R"VG(
# mission_charter.vg (H-04; the second pass 2026-10-10): the mission record (a ship's log out of the people's world: its own sky, the
# moons, the ring, the wanderer, the second sun; the crew's habits, which are the people's) and the charter (how the people of a
# habitat agreed to live, in their own values and faith). The medical log and the memorial are medical_memorial.vg's.

# ---- the mission record -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.mission (words=40..160)
  {mi.head}\n{mi.leg1}\n{mi.leg2}\n{mi.leg3}\n{mi.leg4}\n{mi.end}
  {mi.head}\n{mi.leg1}\n{mi.leg2}\n{mi.leg4}\n{mi.end}
  {mi.head}\n{mi.purpose}\n{mi.leg1}\n{mi.leg3}\n{mi.leg4}\n{mi.end}

mi.head (formula people=4)
  Mission record. Departure from {$home}, cycle {#year:digits}.
  (has:$f) Record of the expedition led by {$f:name}.
  The log of the {mi.ship}, out of {$home}.
  The {mi.ship}, out of {$home}: the record kept aboard.
  Expedition log, cycle {#year:digits}. Crew of {#n}.
  The {~ship}, out of {$home}. Its record.
mi.ship (people=3)
  survey craft
  long ship
  tender to the habitat
  second relay ship
  {colour.holy} ship
  old ferry
  slow boat
  listening ship
  ship of the {festival} crew

mi.purpose
  We go to {mi.target} to {mi.why}.
  The purpose: to {mi.why}, at {mi.target}.
  We are sent to {mi.target}. The assembly says it is to {mi.why}; the crew say it is to get away from the assembly.
mi.target
  (moons>0) {moon}
  the dark rocks
  (giant=1) the wanderer
  (rings=1) the ring
  (companion=1) the second sun
  (comet=1) the hairy star
  the far side of {sun.first}
  the edge of the system
mi.why (share=0.7)
  see whether there is water
  bring back stone for the archive
  leave a marker with all our names on it
  listen, nothing more
  look back at our world from far enough to see the whole of it
  find out where the old signal came from
  plant {crop} where nothing has ever grown
  measure something the machines could measure from home
  take {festival} further than it has ever been
  be the first, which nobody will admit is the reason

mi.leg1
  Day one: {mi.start}. {mi.crew}
  Day [two|three]: {mi.start}.
  Day one: {mi.start}.
mi.leg2
  Day [six|nine|twelve|twenty]: {mi.event}. {mi.crew}
  Day [six|nine|twelve|twenty]: {mi.event}.
mi.leg3
  Day [forty|sixty|eighty]: {mi.event}. {mi.crew}
  Day [forty|sixty|eighty]: {mi.event}.
  (stage>=1) Day [forty|sixty|eighty]: no reply from {$home} in {#n|day}.
mi.leg4
  Day [one hundred and ten|two hundred|three hundred and six]: {mi.far}. {mi.crew}
  Day [one hundred and ten|two hundred|three hundred and six]: {mi.far}.
  (stage>=2) Day [one hundred and ten|two hundred|three hundred and six]: we have decided not to come back. There is nothing to come back to.
mi.start (share=0.7)
  launch, {mi.how}
  the message to {$home}, {mi.how}
  the lights of {city} and the {colour.holy} beacon of {holyplace}, the last we could see of home
  the world, a {colour.any} coin at the window, and somebody crying over the {herd}
  the long sleep for half the crew, {mi.how}
  the {festival} songs from {$home} on the open channel, with {instrument}, until they faded
  {mountain} below us, then the {tree} on its slopes, then only cloud
  the {colour.holy} ribbons tied to the hatch, as the old {people} tied them to boats
  the first meal aboard: {food}, and an argument about it
mi.event
  (2 once) {mi.what}, {mi.how}
  (2 once) {mi.what}, {mi.how}
  (1 once) {mi.saw} through the forward glass
  (1 once) {mi.saw} from the observation ring
  (1 once) {mi.other}
mi.what
  (once) the second burn
  (once) a course correction
  (once) the answer from {$home}
  (once) the repair to the hull
  (once) the sample drill
  (once) the test of the long sleep
  (once) the fire drill
  (once) the {festival} meal, a day late
  (once) the {~instrument} recital, which nobody asked for
  (once) a vote about the music
  (once) the counting of the stores
  (once) the night shift's mutiny over {drink}
mi.far (share=0.7)
  the first sight of our target, {mi.how}
  the survey of the far side, {mi.how}
  the turn for home, {mi.how}
  the telescope found {mi.found}
  a sample taken from the surface, older than anything at home, even the {tree}
  the marker left, cut in {material}, with every name from {$home} on it
  the long look back: our world, a {colour.any} point, and all of us on it
  the signal traced to {mi.found}
mi.how
  nominal
  late, and nobody minded
  small and on time
  {#n|hour} later than planned
  as rehearsed, almost
  done in the dark, by hand
  with an argument first
  better than the machines expected
  in silence, for once
  to applause
  twice, the first time being wrong
mi.saw
  (once) {skyone}, very bright
  (once moons>0) {moon}, closer than anyone has seen it
  (once) something moving in the dark rocks, which was nothing
  (once) {sun.second}, smaller than we have ever seen it
  (once) our own wake of ice, glittering behind us
  (once rings=1) the ring from above, a road of ice to the edge of sight
  (once giant=1) the storms on the wanderer, bigger than our world
  (once companion=1) the second sun rising over the first
  (once aurora=1) the lights over our own pole, from outside
mi.other
  (once) we passed close to {mi.past}, and the instruments sang
  (once) a fault in the water recycler, fixed
  (once) the relay was silent for a day, then back
  (once) we crossed the orbit of {mi.past} and drank {drink} to it
  (once) a dust storm on the hull, all night, like {weather}
mi.past
  (giant=1) the wanderer
  (moons>0) {moon}
  the dark rocks
  (comet=1) the hairy star's path
mi.found
  nothing we were looking for
  something we were not looking for
  the other worlds of {sun.first}, all of them, at last
  a stone with no business being there
  a silence where there should have been noise
mi.crew
  The crew are well.
  {mi.crewone} {mi.crewdid}.
  {mi.crewone} {mi.crewdid}.
  Nobody slept.
mi.crewone (people=4)
  One of them
  The youngest
  The pilot
  The doctor
  Our oldest
  The navigator
  The cook, who is also the engineer
mi.crewdid (share=0.7)
  sings, badly, every night
  keeps a diary and will not let anyone read it
  has started growing {crop2} in a cup
  misses {city} out loud, every evening
  has not spoken in three days, and seems happy
  won the argument about the music
  ate the last of the fresh {fruit}
  plays {fut.game} against the machine and loses
  has painted {motif.over} on the hatch
  swears {oath} at every course correction
  says the dead have {death.went}, and looks out of the window
  keeps a {beast} that nobody admits to bringing
  made {drink} out of something; we are not asking what
  teaches the rest of us {craft} in the off watch

mi.end (formula)
  End of record.
  Next entry when there is something to say.
  End of record. {blessing}.

# ---- the charter ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

genre.charter (words=33..130)
  {ch.head}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.end}
  {ch.head}\n{ch.pre}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.end}
  {ch.head}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.art}\n{ch.end}

ch.head (formula people=3)
  The charter of {$home}, agreed by all who live here, cycle {#year:digits}.
  We who live at {$home} set down how we will live together.
  The charter of {$home}, as read aloud at {festival}.
  How we live at {$home}: agreed in cycle {#year:digits}, to be read every year.
ch.pre (share=0.8)
  We were many once and are fewer now, and we would rather agree over {food} than be ruled.
  This was written in {season.now}, in the {fut.common}, by everyone who came, and the {herd}.
  We hold that {virtue} comes first, and {vice} last; what follows is how.
  The old {people} had laws for everything, even the {herd}; we have kept the few that mattered.

ch.art
  (3 once) Every person has {ch.right}, and no one may take it away.
  (3 once) {ch.own}
  (2 once) No one may be denied {ch.right}.
  (2 once) Every child is taught {ch.teach}, and to look after the {herd}.
  (1 once) {ch.plain}
  (1 once) The {fut.green} belong to everyone.
  (1 once) {festival} is kept by all.
  (1 once) The {herd} in the pens are kept for all, and their keepers fed {food} by all.
  (1 once) No one is to be ashamed of {ch.shame}.
  (1 once) The dead are carried to {deadplace} by those who loved them, and by nobody else.
  (1 once) {ch.value}
  (1 once) What is old is kept: {ch.old}.
  (1 once stage>=1) If the people fall below {nbig}, this charter is to be read again and changed if it must be.
ch.plain (share=0.4)
  The machines serve the people; no machine may decide for a person what the person can decide.
  A disagreement is brought before the assembly, not the machines.
  Anyone may leave. Anyone who leaves may come back.
  What the assembly decides, the assembly can undo.
  No one speaks twice before everyone has spoken once.
ch.own (share=0.8)
  Whoever keeps the {herd} is fed by all; whoever eats is asked to help.
  The {craft} workshops are open to anyone who will clean up after.
  {feast.custom} is kept every year, even if only one of us is left to keep it.
  The {colour.holy} lamps at the {fut.gate} are never put out while anyone lives here.
  No door is painted over; {motif.over} are kept as each family made them.
  The {fut.green} are shared by turns, and the turns are kept by the children.
  Water is given before it is asked for.
  A quarrel over the {fut.green} is settled in the {fut.green}, with the plants listening.
  Every child plants one {tree.n} and is answerable for it.
  The names of the dead are cut at {holyplace} in {colour.holy}, and nowhere else.
  No one eats {food} alone at {festival}.
ch.right (share=0.8)
  (once) a room
  (once) light, water and air
  (once) the right to be left alone
  (once) a voice in the assembly
  (once) a place in the {fut.green}
  (once) the records of their own life
  (once) a seat at {festival}
  (once) a teacher who is a person
  (once) a share of the {crop}
  (once) the right to refuse the machines
ch.teach (share=0.8)
  to read the old records
  to grow food without the machines
  the names of the stars
  the history of {city}
  {craft}, until their hands know it
  the {festival} songs, all of them
  to swim in {river}
  the old words, {~home} first
ch.shame (share=0.6)
  being slow
  being old
  being alone
  not believing
  believing
ch.value
  (value=trade) Every exchange is fair or it is undone.
  (value=trade) What is owed is written down where both can read it, and rubbed out together.
  (value=trade) A price is said aloud, once, and kept; the {fut.common} keeps the scales.
  (value=trade) No one may hold more {crop} than they can eat and trade in a year.
  (value=learning) Every record is open to every person.
  (value=learning) Every child is taught to read the old marks and to doubt them.
  (value=learning) A question asked in the {fut.common} is answered, or written up as not yet answered.
  (value=learning) Whoever knows the {craft} teaches it to anyone who asks, once.
  (value=art) Every person makes something, once a year, for the {fut.common}.
  (value=art) A wall left bare for a year belongs to whoever paints it first, in {colour.any} or any colour.
  (value=art) The {instrument} is played at every meeting before anything is decided.
  (value=art) Nothing made by hand is thrown away; it is given to someone who will keep it.
  (value=war) Every person learns to defend the {fut.gate}, and nobody carries a weapon past it.
  (value=war) The watch is kept by all, by turns, and nobody is excused for age alone.
  (value=war) Old quarrels are settled at the {fut.gate}, in front of witnesses, and then forgotten.
  (value=war) The weapons are kept in one place, under the {colour.holy} cloth, and counted every {season.any}.
  (value=piety) {holyplace} is kept open, and kept quiet.
  (value=piety) The days of {festival} are kept by everyone, and nobody is asked why.
  (value=piety) {rite.imp}, all of us, and the machines stand still while we do.
  (value=piety) The dead are {buried}, as the first ones were, whatever it costs.
ch.old
  the {herd}, the {craft} and the {festival} songs
  {feast.custom}, and the old words
  the names of the dead, and their faces
  {motif.over} on the doors

ch.end (formula)
  Agreed by the assembly. Recorded by the archive.
  Agreed, and sung, at {festival}.
  Agreed by all who came. Those who did not come agree too, by custom.
)VG"
